Abstract = {In this work we describe five new species of Hyalella: Hyalella
   sarukhani sp. nov. from Mexico City, Mexico; H. alvarezi sp. nov., H.
   garyi sp. nov., H. villalobosi sp. nov., and H. viviannae sp. nov. from
   Veracruz, Mexico. Since the four species from Veracruz belong to the H.
   azteca complex due to the form of the telson, here we present a
   morphological comparison using scanning electron microscopy images to
   address the variations within the species.},
